  "question": {
    "text": "A water tank has the shape of an inverted right circular cone, whose semi-vertical angle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math> Water is poured into it at a constant rate of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Then the rate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo></math>in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;at which the level of water is rising at the instant when the depth of water in the tank is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>;</mo></math> is:",
    "image": null
  },
